mono.vendor/patches/luau-lsp/definitions-string-require.patch

Restore string-require resolution after a definitions file declares `require`.

WHY THIS IS A PATCH
    engine.d.luau declares `require: (module: Instance | string) -> any` so an
    instance argument is typed instead of reported as an unknown require. That
    declaration replaces the builtin binding, and with it the "Require" tag and
    Luau's MagicRequire, so a Studio plugin's `require("./core/a")` typed as
    `any`. scriptcheck reattaches the same magic for string arguments only; this
    does the same in the language server, so both checkers agree. It only acts
    when a definitions file replaced the binding, so stock setups are unchanged.

WHERE IT GOES
    src/Workspace.cpp: a StringRequireMagic and restoreStringRequire in an
    anonymous namespace after LUAU_FASTFLAG(LuauSolverV2), and one call per
    globals table in WorkspaceFolder::registerTypes, after the definitions
    files load and before disabled globals are cleared.

WHEN IT STOPS APPLYING
    Re-point the call after registerTypes' definitions loop. Remove this patch
    if upstream keeps require resolution when a definitions file redeclares it.

VALIDATION
    just luau-lsp, then analyze a plugin whose main.luau does
    `local s: string = require("./core/C").n` with core/C.luau returning
    `{ n = 1 }`: it must report a type mismatch. `require(script.Parent.x)`
    must still check without an unknown-require error.

diff --git a/src/Workspace.cpp b/src/Workspace.cpp
--- a/src/Workspace.cpp
+++ b/src/Workspace.cpp
@@ -15,6 +15,47 @@
 
 LUAU_FASTFLAG(LuauSolverV2)
 
+namespace
+{
+// Luau's require magic for a string argument only. Any other argument keeps
+// the signature the definitions file declared.
+struct StringRequireMagic final : Luau::MagicFunction
+{
+    Luau::MagicRequire inner;
+
+    static bool isPath(const Luau::AstExprCall& call)
+    {
+        return call.args.size == 1 && call.args.data[0]->is<Luau::AstExprConstantString>();
+    }
+
+    std::optional<Luau::WithPredicate<Luau::TypePackId>> handleOldSolver(Luau::TypeChecker& checker, const std::shared_ptr<Luau::Scope>& scope,
+        const Luau::AstExprCall& call, Luau::WithPredicate<Luau::TypePackId> arguments) override
+    {
+        if (!isPath(call))
+            return std::nullopt;
+        return inner.handleOldSolver(checker, scope, call, std::move(arguments));
+    }
+
+    bool infer(const Luau::MagicFunctionCallContext& context) override
+    {
+        return isPath(*context.callSite) && inner.infer(context);
+    }
+};
+
+// A definitions file that declares `require` replaces the builtin binding and
+// with it the tags and magic that resolve a string path. Put them back on the
+// declared binding so `require("./a")` types as the module it names.
+void restoreStringRequire(Luau::GlobalTypes& globals)
+{
+    Luau::TypeId require = Luau::getGlobalBinding(globals, "require");
+    if (Luau::hasTag(require, Luau::kRequireTagName))
+        return;
+    Luau::attachTag(require, Luau::kRequireTagName);
+    Luau::attachTag(require, "Require");
+    Luau::attachMagicFunction(require, std::make_shared<StringRequireMagic>());
+}
+} // namespace
+
